<title>USA: Dun &amp; Bradstreet set qtly div $0.25/shr.</title>
<headline>Dun &amp; Bradstreet set qtly div $0.25/shr.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarterly</p>
<p>		   Latest		    Prior</p>
<p> Amount	  $0.25		     $0.25</p>
<p> Pay		Dec 10</p>
<p> Record	   Nov 20</p>
<p>Note: Full name of company is The Dun &amp; Bradstreet Corp. D&amp;B plans to split on Nov 1 into three public companies: Cognizant Corp, ACNielsen Corp, and the &quot;new&quot; Dun &amp; Bradstreet. The dividend attributable to the &quot;new&quot; D&amp;B in the fourth quarter is $0.22/shr, which equates to an annualized rate of $0.88/shr. The dividend attributable to Cognizant in the fourth quarter is $0.03/shr, which equates to an annualized rate of $0.12/shr. As previously announced, ACNielsen will not pay a dividend initially.</p>
</text>
